# .dockerignore
# -------------
# Files and folders excluded from the Docker build context.
# Smaller build context = faster builds, smaller images.
# More importantly: secrets never accidentally end up in the image.

# --- SECRETS (CRITICAL - never bake these into an image) ---
# In production, secrets come from AWS Secrets Manager or
# ECS Task Definition environment variables - never from a file
# baked into the image. If .env ends up in the image, anyone
# who pulls the image can read your AWS credentials.
.env
*.env

# --- Python ---
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# --- Local development artifacts ---
# These are regenerated at runtime from S3/EFS in production
local_index/
sample_docs/

# --- Git ---
.git/
.gitignore

# --- Red-team scripts (not part of the app) ---
redteam_*.py
make_*.py

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db

# --- Tests (not needed in production image) ---
tests/